---

<IndividualPageLayout
    title={seoTitle}
    description={seoDescription}

        modifiedDate={dates.modified}
publishedDate = {dates.published}

    pageTitle={pageTitle}
    heroImage="/media/industry-aerospace-turbine-engine-v5.webp"
    heroImageAlt="industry-aerospace-turbine-engine"
    faqSectionTitle="FAQ: Sourcing Inconel 718 Casting"
    faqItems={faqs}
    ctaTitle="Contact ForceBeyond for an Inconel 718 Technical Quote"
    ctaDescription="Leverage our co-owned global network for your next superalloy project. Our engineering headquarters in Newark, Delaware, provides a seamless bridge to our advanced production assets in Asia and the US."
    sourcesTitle="Sources"
    sourcesList={sources}
    resourcesTitle="Related Inconel 718 & Superalloy Casting Resources"
    resourcesList={internalResources}
>
    <div class="individual-content ">
        <p>
            <strong>Inconel 718 Casting Key Facts:</strong> Inconel 718 (UNS N07718) is a precipitation-hardenable nickel-based superalloy that may be investment cast to applicable specifications such as AMS 5383. ForceBeyond supports vacuum investment casting using VIM for applicable routes, HIP where required, heat treatment, NDT, and precision 5-axis CNC machining. Published elevated-temperature property data extend to approximately 1300°F (704°C), while actual allowable service conditions depend on material condition, geometry, loading, environment, qualification requirements, and the governing specification.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div slot="full-width" class="individual-content">

        <section id="overview" >
            <div class="content-container">
                
                <h2>Inconel 718 Casting: High-Precision Manufacturing in USA, South Korea & Taiwan</h2>

                <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center mt-6">
                    <div>
                        <p>
                           ForceBeyond is a specialized <strong>Inconel 718 casting supplier</strong> providing mission-critical components for aerospace, 
                           space exploration, and power generation. Through our <strong>co-owned foundry network in the USA, South Korea, and Taiwan</strong>, 
                           we deliver high-strength, corrosion-resistant Inconel 718 parts utilizing advanced Vacuum Induction Melting (VIM) technology. 
                           Our manufacturing model combines US-based engineering support with production capacity across the network to improve supply-chain resilience. The current capability statement includes casting sizes up to 32 inches, weights from 0.02 to 220 pounds, and typical casting tolerances from ISO 8062 CT7 to CT5 / VDG P690 D1 to D2, subject to geometry and process review. As part of our broader <a href="/high-performance-superalloy-casting/" class="highlight-link">Superalloy Casting Services</a> expertise, HIP may be applied when required to reduce internal microporosity. Final acceptance is controlled by the applicable drawing, material specification, inspection plan, qualification requirements, and customer requirements.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="relative">
                        <div class="overflow-hidden">
                            <img
                                src="/media/Gas-Turbine-Impeller-sku-3.webp"
                                alt="Gas-Turbine-Impeller-sku-3"
                                class="w-full h-auto object-cover hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
                            />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="properties-table">
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Technical Specifications: Precision Inconel 718 Properties</h2>
                <p>
                        ForceBeyond supports Inconel 718 investment casting programs to applicable
                        material specifications such as <strong>AMS 5383</strong>. The governing
                        specification, revision, heat-treatment condition, mechanical-property requirements,
                        and inspection criteria are controlled by the customer drawing and purchase order. 
                        We provide full material traceability (MTRs) and NDT reports with every 
                        shipment to verify mechanical integrity.
                    </p>
                <div class="content-table-wrapper">
                    <table>

                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Alloy Grade</th>
                                <th scope="col">Value (Typical Cast & Aged)</th>

                            </tr>
                        </thead>

                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Tensile strength</th>
                                <td>125,000 psi (860 MPa)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Yield strength(0.2% offset)</th>
                                <td>110,000 psi (760 MPa)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Elongation</th>
                                <td>5% – 10%</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Elevated-temperature reference</th>
                                <td>Published property data extend to approximately 1300°F (704°C); allowable service conditions are application- and specification-dependent.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="Why Forcebeyond" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Why Partner with ForceBeyond for Inconel 718 Casting?</h2>
                
                <p>
                    A stable supply of Inconel 718 requires more than just a vendor; it requires a manufacturing partner with direct oversight.
                </p>
                
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>VIM (Vacuum Induction Melting) Expertise:</strong> VIM helps limit oxidation, gas pickup, and contamination during melting of Inconel 718, supporting alloy cleanliness and consistency. Final microstructure and fatigue performance also depend on casting conditions, heat treatment, HIP where required, defects, surface condition, geometry, and service environment.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Direct Co-Owned Operational Control:</strong> We eliminate the “broker gap.” By <strong>co-owning our foundries</strong> in the US, South Korea, and Taiwan, ForceBeyond manages the Quality Management System (QMS) and production scheduling directly, ensuring prioritized lead times.
                    <li>
                        <strong>Near-Net-Shape Accuracy:</strong> Our investment casting process achieves tight tolerances, significantly reducing the cost of secondary machining on high-hardness Inconel 718 alloys.
                </ul>

                <p>
                    Hot Isostatic Pressing (HIP) for Internal Porosity Control
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Hot Isostatic Pressing (HIP)</strong> may be applied when required by the drawing, material specification, qualification plan, customer requirements, or service conditions. HIP can reduce internal microporosity and increase density, but it does not create a universal zero-defect condition or make cast and forged material interchangeable. Final fatigue and structural performance remain dependent on material condition, casting quality, heat treatment, geometry, surface condition, defects, inspection acceptance criteria, and service environment.
                </p>

            </div>
        </section>


        <section id="Tier-1.5-Integration">
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Tier-1.5 Integration: Precision Cast-to-Machine Solutions</h2>
                
                <p>
                    ForceBeyond provides a seamless transition from <strong>Vacuum Investment Casting</strong> to finished print dimensions. 
                    Because Inconel 718 is exceptionally hard to machine (up to 44 HRC after aging), 
                    our Tier-1.5 model integrates our casting foundries with our specialized <a href="/inconel-718-machining" class="highlight-link">Inconel 718 Machining</a> centers.
                </p>

                <p>
                    By coordinating casting, heat treatment, inspection, and 5-axis CNC machining within one sourcing program, ForceBeyond can reduce avoidable dimensional hand-off risk. Proof machining and inspection planning may be used where appropriate to establish datum features and support downstream NDT or finish machining. Facility certifications and final acceptance requirements are confirmed for the selected production route and customer program.
                </p>

                <p>
                    For components requiring superior grain flow over complex internal geometries, 
                    explore our integrated <a href="/inconel-718-forging" class="highlight-link">Inconel 718 Forging</a> solutions.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>


        <section id="certified-applications" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Representative Inconel 718 Casting Applications</h2>
                
                <p>
                   Inconel 718 castings may be considered for demanding applications such as:
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Aerospace:</strong> Turbine blades, compressor casings, and structural segments.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Space Exploration:</strong> Rocket engine manifolds and turbopump hardware.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Power Generation:</strong> Industrial gas-turbine components and selected nuclear/SMR hardware where permitted by the governing specification, qualification plan, code, and customer requirements.
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>


        


        <section id="quality-assurance" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Quality Assurance & Certification Standards</h2>
                <p>
                    Documentation and inspection are provided according to the applicable drawing, purchase order, material specification, qualification plan, and customer requirements. Where AMS 5383 is invoked, the applicable revision and acceptance requirements control.
                </p>
                <div class="content-table-wrapper">
                    <table>

                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Inspection Method</th>
                                <th scope="col">Purpose for Inconel 718 Casting</th>
                                <th scope="col">Standard Compliance</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>

                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Radiographic Testing (RT)</th>
                                <td>X-ray inspection to detect internal shrinkage or inclusions.</td>
                                <td>ASTM E192 / ASTM E1030</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Fluorescent Penetrant (FPI)</th>
                                <td>Identifying surface-breaking porosity or cracks.</td>
                                <td>ASTM E1417 or applicable customer requirement</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Spectrographic Analysis</th>
                                <td>Verifying chemical balance (Ni, Cr, Fe, Nb, Mo, Ti, Al).</td>
                                <td>ASTM E1476</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Mechanical Testing</th>
                                <td>Room temperature and elevated temperature tensile testing.</td>
                                <td>ASTM E8 / ASTM E21</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</IndividualPageLayout>